// =============================================================================
// partnerships-course — "Partnerships: Who You Build With"
// =============================================================================
// Course six of the Real Estate department. Five courses covered the ground,
// the stewardship, the transaction, the tenant and the building. This one
// covers the person standing next to you when you sign.
//
// THE ARC, one argument in eight moves:
//   1. Can two walk together, except they be agreed? (Amos 3:3)
//   2. Two are better than one (Ecclesiastes 4:9, 10, 12)
//   3. Unequally yoked: what a yoke actually is (2 Corinthians 6:14)
//   4. And the ships were broken (2 Chronicles 20:35-37; 1 Kings 22:48)
//   5. Let there be no strife: separate thyself (Genesis 13:8, 9)
//   6. The contention was so sharp (Acts 15:39, 40)
//   7. In the multitude of counsellors (Proverbs 15:22)
//   8. The people had a mind to work (Nehemiah 4:6)
//
// Agree before you walk -> know why partnership is worth it at all -> know what
// a yoke actually is -> weigh the counterparty, not only the deal -> settle the
// ending while you can still afford to be generous -> know that an ending is
// not a sin -> get the wisdom without the yoke -> and the thing no document
// produces. Lesson 8 is last because the seven before it are technique applied
// to other people, and it turns the question round.
//
// THE COURSE'S OWN BALANCE, held deliberately. Lesson 2 makes the case FOR
// partnership BEFORE any warning arrives, because a curriculum that only
// cautions is teaching suspicion rather than the Word. Lesson 6 then refuses
// the opposite error: Scripture records a sharp separation and assigns fault to
// NEITHER man, which forecloses the reading that would keep an operator yoked
// past usefulness because leaving has been made to feel like betrayal.
//
// THE DEPARTMENT'S RECURRING SHAPE, a sixth time: a wrong invisible from inside
// any single instance. The false weight, the lawful process that took Naboth's
// vineyard, attrition on a promise, the seating chart, the daub -- and now the
// disagreement that existed on day one, unstated, whose price only rose.
//
// THE LINE THIS COURSE HOLDS (DR-0098). Lesson 4 is the hardest: a genuinely
// good king joined one venture with a wicked one and the text names the
// COUNTERPARTY as the cause. The limit is stated in the lesson itself, because
// overstated this becomes superstition -- not every failed venture reveals a
// bad partner. The claim is narrower: a sound business is no protection against
// an unsound partner, and in practice the deal is modelled while the person is
// assumed.
//
// NO PASSAGE IS SHARED with any of the department's other five courses, and the
// course test CHECKS that against their own reference lists. All nine are fresh
// ground against the 64 book-and-chapters already in use.
//
// BANDS, BENEFITS AND STORIES FROM THE FIRST COMMIT. Every lesson carries
// levels.teen and levels.senior (DR-0497/0498), five or six `benefits`, and two
// `stories`. That last pair is new to this course and is why DR-0509 exists:
// the send stage's reader-facing side carries ONLY benefits and the teach
// stage's carries ONLY stories, so five earlier courses rendered a heading with
// nothing under it. Darrell found it in the app before any gate did. The
// generator now refuses to emit a course without them and
// every-stage-reaches-the-reader fails one that ships bare.
//
// VERIFICATION (DR-0076 / SCRIPTURE-REFERENCE-STANDARD). All 58 quoted spans
// fetched VERBATIM from the repository's own KJV. The generator caught 12 stray
// backslashes and 2 straight apostrophes before emitting; the first repair
// attempt GUESSED which strings were affected and fixed the wrong ones, so all
// 13 remaining defects were then located programmatically in one pass. Our
// prose says Yahweh; quotations keep "God" and "the LORD" exactly as the KJV
// has them (DR-0210's bright line).
//
// TEACHING, NOT LEGAL ADVICE -- carried on the meta. Entity selection,
// shareholder and partnership agreements, personal guarantees, fiduciary duty
// and dissolution are jurisdiction specific and they change.
// =============================================================================

